  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read in pg_dump via an over-long\n     pg_proc.protrftypes array\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19385.patch: have parseOidArray() allocate the\n       array itself and size it from its input instead of trusting a\n       caller-supplied FUNC_MAX_ARGS bound, reject a list that is too short or\n       too long, split out parseIntArray() for signed attribute numbers, drop\n       the fixed FUNC_MAX_ARGS allocation in dumpFunc() and cover the TRANSFORM\n       dump path in the regression tests, in src/bin/pg_dump/common.c,\n       src/bin/pg_dump/pg_dump.c, src/bin/pg_dump/pg_dump.h,\n       src/test/regress/expected/object_address.out and\n       src/test/regress/sql/object_address.sql\n     - CVE-2026-19385",
